      en: "North Point is a district on the eastern shore of Hong Kong Island, characterized by its dense urban fabric and waterfront. Historically a middle-class residential area, it became a hub for the Fujianese community in the 1950s. The district is known for its traditional shops and eateries along King's Road. The North Point Ferry Pier connects to Kowloon. Cultural landmarks include the Tin Hau Temple, built in the 1870s, and the North Point Public Park. With a population density exceeding 180,000 per km², it is one of the most densely populated areas in Hong Kong. The district also houses the Hong Kong Film Archive.",
